# Golden vectors of func_8006C080 (gDrawThreeSlotStatusBar), the three-slot HUD status bar.
#
# Generated by running the ORIGINAL src/game/8006C080.c, src/game/8006BF44.c and
# src/game/800491F8.c in the host harness tests/host/slots/h.c against tests/host/slots/states.txt;
# only the MIPS __asm__ register/address attributes were stripped and the (u32) pointer casts in
# 8006C080.c widened to (unsigned long) so the code runs on 64-bit hosts.
#
# Each CASE line echoes the input state (player +0xC1, frameTime, gPlayerInvulnerable[c1],
# gSinglePlayerEntity != 0, player +0x84[0..2], player +0x8A[0..2], player +0x90[0..2]), followed
# by the calls recorded in order:
#
#   REGISTRY id                                              gRegistryFind(field90[i])
#   TEXT ".." x y colour                                     func_800491F8 -> gDrawAlignedString
#   packetN code=.. len=.. rgb=.. xy=.. uv=.. clut=.. wh=..  packets emitted by func_8006BF44
#
# The harness sets gEnvMapTexpageWord[0] = 0x7C00 | (0x1234 << 16) and gFormatStringB = "%ld".
# A PS1 long is 32 bits wide, so "%ld" is an ordinary signed conversion: the final case passes -1
# and the retail code prints "-1". The host harness rewrites "%ld" to its int form for that reason
# (a 64-bit host long would read past the passed int); see tests/host/slots/h.c.
#
# Regenerate or re-check with tests/host/slots/slots_test.sh (--emit prints the observed output;
# without it the script compares this file against a fresh run of the retail routines).

CASE c1=0 frame=0x0 inv=0 second=0 counts84=1,2,3 counts8A=4,5,6 ids=7,8,9
